10
01:13:53,333 --> 01:13:59,333
The Ninth Gate is a 1999 neo-noir horror thriller film
directed, produced, and co-written by Roman Polanski.

11
01:21:16,666 --> 01:21:22,666
An international co-production between the United States, Portugal, France, and Spain, the
film is loosely based upon Arturo Pérez-Reverte's 1993 novel The Club Dumas.

12
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
The film stars Johnny Depp as a dealer of rare books who is tasked with
authenticating a 17th-century book that, if used correctly, can summon the Devil.

13
01:36:03,333 --> 01:36:09,333
The premiere showing was at San Sebastián, Spain, on 25 August 1999, a month
before the 47th San Sebastian International Film Festival.

14
01:43:26,666 --> 01:43:32,666
Though critically and commercially unsuccessful in North America, where reviewers compared it unfavorably with Polanski's supernatural
film Rosemary's Baby (1968), The Ninth Gate earned a worldwide gross of $58.4 million against a $38 million budget.

15
01:50:50,000 --> 01:50:56,000
It has since been described as a cult classic.

16
01:58:13,333 --> 01:58:19,333
The film explores themes of hotel, new york city, suicide, library, portugal.

17
02:05:36,666 --> 02:05:42,666
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
